-- @@ L10-29 verbatim
/-!
# Base change of projective space

A ring map `f : R →+* A` induces (`Proj.map` of `MvPolynomial.map f`) a morphism
`map f : ℙ(n; A) ⟶ ℙ(n; R)` over `Spec A ⟶ Spec R`. It pulls back the standard opens `U i` to
`U i`, is `Spec` of `MvPolynomial.map f : R[Y] → A[Y]` in the standard charts, and exhibits
`ℙ(n; A)` as the base change `ℙ(n; R) ×_{Spec R} Spec A`. The standard cocycle `(Xⱼ / Xᵢ)`
defining the twisting sheaves pulls back to the standard cocycle.

## Main definitions and results

- `ProjectiveSpace.map f : ℙ(n; A) ⟶ ℙ(n; R)`, with `map_id`, `map_comp`, `map_preimage_U`,
  `map_toSpec`.
- `ProjectiveSpace.chart_comp_map`: `chart i ≫ map f = Spec.map (MvPolynomial.map f) ≫ chart i`.
- `ProjectiveSpace.isPullback_map`: **base change**, `ℙ(n; A) = ℙ(n; R) ×_{Spec R} Spec A`;
  `ProjectiveSpace.baseChangeIso` is the resulting isomorphism.
- `ProjectiveSpace.map_appLE_xDiv`: `(map f)^♯ (Xⱼ / Xᵢ) = Xⱼ / Xᵢ`.
- `ProjectiveSpace.cocycle_isPullback`: the standard cocycle of `ℙ(n; A)` is the pullback of the
  standard cocycle of `ℙ(n; R)`.
-/


